  "_comment": "The two scanners the scan job downloads, pinned by version, URL and sha256 (design spec §8.1). A download whose sha256 differs is refused and that tool's coverage is `failed` / `fetch_failed`. linux-x64 is what ubuntu-latest runs; linux-arm64 serves ARM runners; the darwin entries exist so the fixture tests can run the same pinned binaries on a developer's Mac. Every sha256 was read on 2026-09-30 from the GitHub release's asset digest AND the release's own checksum file (gitleaks_8.30.1_checksums.txt, osv-scanner_SHA256SUMS); both agreed. `defaultConfig` is Gitleaks' default rule set at the pinned tag: the release script derives each release's `ruleIds` from it, because gitleaks.toml extends it (`useDefault = true`).",
